><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mopen nulldelimiter\"></span><span class=\"mfrac\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.8451em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.655em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">2</span></span></span></span><span style=\"top:-3.23em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"frac-line\" style=\"border-bottom-width:0.04em;\"></span></span><span style=\"top:-3.394em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">1</span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.345em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mclose nulldelimiter\"></span></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">ρ</span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">c</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.3361em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:0em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">d</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">A</span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0359em;\">v</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.8141em;\"><span style=\"top:-3.063em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">2</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span> take their share first; the motor and inverter lose a fraction <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.7278em;vertical-align:-0.0833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">1</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">−</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.625em;vertical-align:-0.1944em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0359em;\">η</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.1514em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:-0.0359em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">m</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0359em;\">η</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.3117em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:-0.0359em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">in</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\" style=\"margin-right:0.0359em;\">v</span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span> of the rest, the battery another <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.7278em;vertical-align:-0.0833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">1</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">−</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.625em;vertical-align:-0.1944em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0359em;\">η</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.3361em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:-0.0359em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">ba</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">t</span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span>. If the braking power exceeds the battery’s charge limit (cold cells, a full battery), the excess must go to friction brakes or a braking resistor. Writing the books this way, and checking they close, catches sign errors and missing terms in any energy model.</p>\n<h2 id=\"mountain-descents\">Mountain descents</h2>\n<p>Mountain railways and cable cars, common in Switzerland, are the textbook case: a long, steady descent with a heavy vehicle. Recovered energy can feed other trains on the line or a battery, and a vehicle that brakes electrically wears its friction brakes far less. The numbers below are for an illustrative car, not a specific line.</p>\n\n<figure class=\"fig\"><div class=\"fig-body\"><div class=\"widget\" data-widget=\"regenbooks\" data-args=\"{}\"></div></div><figcaption>Energy accounts for the descent. Change the grade, speed, efficiencies and battery charge limit; the bars show where the potential energy goes.</figcaption></figure>\n<h2 id=\"worked-example\">Worked example</h2>\n<p>A 40 t car descends 500 m on a 10 % grade at 10 m/s, with motor 93 %, inverter 97 % and battery 95 % efficiency and a 400 kW charge limit:</p>\n<ol>\n<li>Potential energy released: 54.500 kWh.</li>\n<li>Stored 82.9 %, motor and inverter losses 9.5 %, battery losses 4.4 %, rolling resistance 2.0 %, air drag 1.2 %, friction brakes 0.1 % (only the final stop exceeds the charge limit).</li>\n<li>The accounts close to within 0.005 % of the total (the time-step error).</li>\n<li>With a 100 kW charge limit, only 26.2 % is stored and 66.2 % goes to friction brakes.</li>\n</ol>\n<h2 id=\"code-it-from-scratch\">Code it from scratch</h2>\n\n<div class=\"code-card\" data-code=\"0\"><div class=\"code-head\"><span class=\"fname\" translate=\"no\">regen.py</span><button class=\"btn btn-quiet btn-small\" type=\"button\" data-copy=\"0\">Copy</button><button class=\"btn btn-quiet btn-small\" type=\"button\" data-download=\"0\">Download</button></div><pre tabindex=\"0\"><code class=\"language-python\"><span class=\"hljs-keyword\">import</span> numpy <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">as</span> np\n\nG = <span class=\"hljs-number\">9.81</span>\n\n<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">def</span> <span class=\"hljs-title function_\">descent</span>(<span class=\"hljs-params\">m=<span class=\"hljs-number\">40e3</span>, h=<span class=\"hljs-number\">500.0</span>, grade=<span class=\"hljs-number\">0.10</span>, v_set=<span class=\"hljs-number\">10.0</span>, crr=<span class=\"hljs-number\">0.002</span>, cda=<span class=\"hljs-number\">8.0</span>, rho=<span class=\"hljs-number\">1.2</span>, eta_m=<span class=\"hljs-number\">0.93</span>, eta_inv=<span class=\"hljs-number\">0.97</span>, eta_bat=<span class=\"hljs-number\">0.95</span>,\n            p_bat_max=<span class=\"hljs-number\">400e3</span>, a_max=<span class=\"hljs-number\">0.5</span>, dt=<span class=\"hljs-number\">0.05</span></span>):\n    <span class=\"hljs-string\">&quot;&quot;&quot;a vehicle descends a constant grade from rest to rest. A speed controller asks the motor for braking force; the\n    motor turns it into electrical power (eta_m, eta_inv), the battery stores it (eta_bat) up to its charge limit, and\n    friction brakes take whatever the electric system cannot. Every joule is booked to one account.&quot;&quot;&quot;</span>\n    th = np.arctan(grade); L = h / np.sin(th); x = v = <span class=\"hljs-number\">0.0</span>; acc = <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">dict</span>.fromkeys([<span class=\"hljs-string\">&quot;rolling&quot;</span>, <span class=\"hljs-string\">&quot;aero&quot;</span>, <span class=\"hljs-string\">&quot;motor+inverter loss&quot;</span>, <span class=\"hljs-string\">&quot;battery loss&quot;</span>, <span class=\"hljs-string\">&quot;stored&quot;</span>, <span class=\"hljs-string\">&quot;friction brakes&quot;</span>], <span class=\"hljs-number\">0.0</span>)\n    <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">while</span> x &lt; L:\n        stop = v**<span class=\"hljs-number\">2</span> / (<span class=\"hljs-number\">2</span> * a_max)                                             <span class=\"hljs-comment\"># distance needed to stop at a_max</span>\n        v_ref = <span class=\"hljs-number\">0.0</span> <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">if</span> L - x &lt;= stop <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">else</span> v_set\n        f_grav = m * G * np.sin(th); f_roll = crr * m * G * np.cos(th); f_aero = <span class=\"hljs-number\">0.5</span> * rho * cda * v**<span class=\"hljs-number\">2</span>\n        a_want = np.clip((v_ref - v) / <span class=\"hljs-number\">2.0</span>, -a_max, a_max)                    <span class=\"hljs-comment\"># gentle speed controller</span>\n        f_brake = <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">max</span>(<span class=\"hljs-number\">0.0</span>, f_grav - f_roll - f_aero - m * a_want)            <span class=\"hljs-comment\"># total braking force needed</span>\n        p_mech = f_brake * v; p_elec = p_mech * eta_m * eta_inv; p_bat = <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">min</span>(p_elec, p_bat_max / eta_bat)\n        p_store = p_bat * eta_bat; p_fric = (p_elec - p_bat) / (eta_m * eta_inv)   <span class=\"hljs-comment\"># excess handed back to friction brakes</span>\n        a = (f_grav - f_roll - f_aero - f_brake) / m\n        acc[<span class=\"hljs-string\">&quot;rolling&quot;</span>] += f_roll * v * dt; acc[<span class=\"hljs-string\">&quot;aero&quot;</span>] += f_aero * v * dt\n        acc[<span class=\"hljs-string\">&quot;motor+inverter loss&quot;</span>] += (p_mech - p_fric) * (<span class=\"hljs-number\">1</span> - eta_m * eta_inv) * dt\n        acc[<span class=\"hljs-string\">&quot;battery loss&quot;</span>] += p_bat * (<span class=\"hljs-number\">1</span> - eta_bat) * dt; acc[<span class=\"hljs-string\">&quot;stored&quot;</span>] += p_store * dt; acc[<span class=\"hljs-string\">&quot;friction brakes&quot;</span>] += p_fric * dt\n        v_new = <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">max</span>(v + a * dt, <span class=\"hljs-number\">0.0</span>); x += <span class=\"hljs-number\">0.5</span> * (v + v_new) * dt; v = v_new\n        <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">if</span> v == <span class=\"hljs-number\">0.0</span> <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">and</span> v_ref == <span class=\"hljs-number\">0.0</span>: <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">break</span>\n    pe = m * G * x * np.sin(th)\n    <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">return</span> pe, acc, <span class=\"hljs-number\">0.5</span> * m * v**<span class=\"hljs-number\">2</span>\n\n<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">def</span> <span class=\"hljs-title function_\">test_accounting_closes</span>():\n    pe, acc, ke = descent()\n    <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">print</span>(<span class=\"hljs-string\">f&quot;potential energy released <span class=\"hljs-subst\">{pe / <span class=\"hljs-number\">3.6e6</span>:<span class=\"hljs-number\">.3</span>f}</span> kWh&quot;</span>)\n    <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">for</span> k, val <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">in</span> acc.items(): <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">print</span>(<span class=\"hljs-string\">f&quot;  <span class=\"hljs-subst\">{k:22s}</span> <span class=\"hljs-subst\">{val / <span class=\"hljs-number\">3.6e6</span>:<span class=\"hljs-number\">7.3</span>f}</span> kWh (<span class=\"hljs-subst\">{<span class=\"hljs-number\">100</span> * val / pe:<span class=\"hljs-number\">5.1</span>f}</span> %)&quot;</span>)\n    gap = pe - <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">sum</span>(acc.values()) - ke\n    <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">print</span>(<span class=\"hljs-string\">f&quot;accounting gap <span class=\"hljs-subst\">{gap / <span class=\"hljs-number\">3.6e6</span>:<span class=\"hljs-number\">.2</span>e}</span> kWh (<span class=\"hljs-subst\">{<span class=\"hljs-number\">100</span> * <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">abs</span>(gap) / pe:<span class=\"hljs-number\">.3</span>f}</span> % of the total)&quot;</span>)\n    <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">assert</span> <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">abs</span>(gap) / pe &lt; <span class=\"hljs-number\">5e-4</span> <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">and</span> acc[<span class=\"hljs-string\">&quot;friction brakes&quot;</span>] &lt; <span class=\"hljs-number\">0.01</span> * pe       <span class=\"hljs-comment\"># only the final stop exceeds the charge limit</span>\n\n<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">def</span> <span class=\"hljs-title function_\">test_battery_limit</span>():\n    pe, acc, _ = descent(p_bat_max=<span class=\"hljs-number\">100e3</span>)\n    <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">print</span>(<span class=\"hljs-string\">f&quot;with a 100 kW charge limit: stored <span class=\"hljs-subst\">{<span class=\"hljs-number\">100</span> * acc[<span class=\"hljs-string\">&#x27;stored&#x27;</span>] / pe:<span class=\"hljs-number\">.1</span>f}</span> %, friction brakes <span class=\"hljs-subst\">{<span class=\"hljs-number\">100</span> * acc[<span class=\"hljs-string\">&#x27;friction brakes&#x27;</span>] / pe:<span class=\"hljs-number\">.1</span>f}</span> %&quot;</span>)\n    <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">assert</span> acc[<span class=\"hljs-string\">&quot;friction brakes&quot;</span>] &gt; <span class=\"hljs-number\">0</span> <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">and</span> acc[<span class=\"hljs-string\">&quot;stored&quot;</span>] &lt; descent()[<span class=\"hljs-number\">1</span>][<span class=\"hljs-string\">&quot;stored&quot;</span>]\n\ntest_accounting_closes()\ntest_battery_limit()\n<span class=\"hljs-built_in\">print</span>(<span class=\"hljs-string\">&quot;PASS&quot;</span>)</code></pre></div>\n<h2 id=\"in-practice\">In practice</h2>\n<p>NumPy is all an energy-accounting model needs; it is the first step in sizing a battery or braking resistor. Vehicle and rail engineers use the same books in tools such as MATLAB/Simulink or OpenTrack, add the drive’s efficiency maps against torque and speed, and model the battery’s charge-power limit against temperature and state of charge, which is often what limits recovery in practice.</p>\n<h2 id=\"exercises\">Exercises</h2>\n\n<div class=\"exercise\"><div class=\"ex-q\"><p>How much energy is released by a 40 t car descending 500 m, in kWh?</p>\n</div><details><summary>Show the solution</summary><div class=\"ex-s\"><p><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.8889em;vertical-align:-0.1944em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">m</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0359em;\">g</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">h</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.7278em;vertical-align:-0.0833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">40000</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">×</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.7278em;vertical-align:-0.0833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">9.81</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">×</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">500</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">196.2</span></span></span></span> MJ <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.3669em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">54.5</span></span></span></span> kWh.</p>\n</div></details></div>\n\n<div class=\"exercise\"><div class=\"ex-q\"><p>Why does a full battery force the friction brakes to work?</p>\n</div><details><summary>Show the solution</summary><div class=\"ex-s\"><p>A full battery cannot accept charge, so its charge limit drops to zero. Every joule the motor would generate has nowhere to go, so the controller must brake by friction or dump the energy in a braking resistor.</p>\n</div></details></div>\n<h2 id=\"quiz\">Quiz</h2>\n\n<div class=\"quiz\" data-quiz=\"p19-l09\"></div>\n","toc":[{"id":"braking-as-generation","title":"Braking as generation"},{"id":"where-the-energy-goes","title":"Where the energy goes"},{"id":"mountain-descents","title":"Mountain descents"},{"id":"worked-example","title":"Worked example"},{"id":"code-it-from-scratch","title":"Code it from scratch"},{"id":"in-practice","title":"In practice"},{"id":"exercises","title":"Exercises"},{"id":"quiz","title":"Quiz"}],"quiz":[{"id":"p19-l09-q1","type":"num","q":"<p>Potential energy of 10 t descending 200 m (kWh)?</p>\n","explain":"<p>m g h divided by 3.6 MJ per kWh.</p>\n","answer":5.45,"tol":0.01,"unit":""},{"id":"p19-l09-q2","type":"num","q":"<p>Fraction stored from mechanical braking with 93 %, 97 % and 95 % efficiencies (%)?</p>\n","explain":"<p>Multiply the efficiencies.</p>\n","answer":85.7,"tol":0.01,"unit":""},{"id":"p19-l09-q3","type":"num","q":"<p>Braking power for 20 kN at 15 m/s (kW)?</p>\n","explain":"<p>P = F v.</p>\n","answer":300,"tol":0.001,"unit":""},{"id":"p19-l09-q4","type":"num","q":"<p>Air drag power with cdA 8 m², ρ 1.2 kg/m³ at 10 m/s (kW)?</p>\n","explain":"<p>½ρ cdA v³.</p>\n","answer":4.8,"tol":0.01,"unit":""},{"id":"p19-l09-q5","type":"mc","q":"<p>What happens to braking energy the battery cannot accept?</p>\n","explain":"<p>The excess must be dissipated somewhere.</p>\n","options":["It is stored in the motor","It goes to friction brakes or a braking resistor","It disappears","It raises the bus voltage harmlessly forever"],"answer":1},{"id":"p19-l09-q6","type":"mc","q":"<p>Why check that the energy accounts close?</p>\n","explain":"<p>Every joule must be booked once.</p>\n","options":["It catches sign errors and missing loss terms","It makes the battery larger","It speeds up the simulation","It is required by the motor"],"answer":0}],"code":[{"file":"regen.py","lang":"python","src":"import numpy as np\n\nG = 9.81\n\ndef descent(m=40e3, h=500.0, grade=0.10, v_set=10.0, crr=0.002, cda=8.0, rho=1.2, eta_m=0.93, eta_inv=0.97, eta_bat=0.95,\n            p_bat_max=400e3, a_max=0.5, dt=0.05):\n    \"\"\"a vehicle descends a constant grade from rest to rest. A speed controller asks the motor for braking force; the\n    motor turns it into electrical power (eta_m, eta_inv), the battery stores it (eta_bat) up to its charge limit, and\n    friction brakes take whatever the electric system cannot. Every joule is booked to one account.\"\"\"\n    th = np.arctan(grade); L = h / np.sin(th); x = v = 0.0; acc = dict.fromkeys([\"rolling\", \"aero\", \"motor+inverter loss\", \"battery loss\", \"stored\", \"friction brakes\"], 0.0)\n    while x < L:\n        stop = v**2 / (2 * a_max)                                             # distance needed to stop at a_max\n        v_ref = 0.0 if L - x <= stop else v_set\n        f_grav = m * G * np.sin(th); f_roll = crr * m * G * np.cos(th); f_aero = 0.5 * rho * cda * v**2\n        a_want = np.clip((v_ref - v) / 2.0, -a_max, a_max)                    # gentle speed controller\n        f_brake = max(0.0, f_grav - f_roll - f_aero - m * a_want)            # total braking force needed\n        p_mech = f_brake * v; p_elec = p_mech * eta_m * eta_inv; p_bat = min(p_elec, p_bat_max / eta_bat)\n        p_store = p_bat * eta_bat; p_fric = (p_elec - p_bat) / (eta_m * eta_inv)   # excess handed back to friction brakes\n        a = (f_grav - f_roll - f_aero - f_brake) / m\n        acc[\"rolling\"] += f_roll * v * dt; acc[\"aero\"] += f_aero * v * dt\n        acc[\"motor+inverter loss\"] += (p_mech - p_fric) * (1 - eta_m * eta_inv) * dt\n        acc[\"battery loss\"] += p_bat * (1 - eta_bat) * dt; acc[\"stored\"] += p_store * dt; acc[\"friction brakes\"] += p_fric * dt\n        v_new = max(v + a * dt, 0.0); x += 0.5 * (v + v_new) * dt; v = v_new\n        if v == 0.0 and v_ref == 0.0: break\n    pe = m * G * x * np.sin(th)\n    return pe, acc, 0.5 * m * v**2\n\ndef test_accounting_closes():\n    pe, acc, ke = descent()\n    print(f\"potential energy released {pe / 3.6e6:.3f} kWh\")\n    for k, val in acc.items(): print(f\"  {k:22s} {val / 3.6e6:7.3f} kWh ({100 * val / pe:5.1f} %)\")\n    gap = pe - sum(acc.values()) - ke\n    print(f\"accounting gap {gap / 3.6e6:.2e} kWh ({100 * abs(gap) / pe:.3f} % of the total)\")\n    assert abs(gap) / pe < 5e-4 and acc[\"friction brakes\"] < 0.01 * pe       # only the final stop exceeds the charge limit\n\ndef test_battery_limit():\n    pe, acc, _ = descent(p_bat_max=100e3)\n    print(f\"with a 100 kW charge limit: stored {100 * acc['stored'] / pe:.1f} %, friction brakes {100 * acc['friction brakes'] / pe:.1f} %\")\n    assert acc[\"friction brakes\"] > 0 and acc[\"stored\"] < descent()[1][\"stored\"]\n\ntest_accounting_closes()\ntest_battery_limit()\nprint(\"PASS\")"}]}